-- spellings.txt --
AIGW  Action required
────────────────────────────────────────

Problem
  unknown option --model; run `aigw setup --help`

Fix
  aigw setup --help
-- rejected.txt --
sk-rejected-token
-- token.txt --
sk-team-token-0001
-- help.txt --
AIGW  aigw setup
────────────────────────────────────────
  Without --from, ask in a terminal for a provider, an installed client and a model from the
  provider's catalog, save them, and check the client; it can run again. With --from, apply a
  team file: its models, families and recommendations win, and an existing provider keeps its
  endpoints and Token.

Usage
  aigw setup [flags]

Examples
  aigw setup
  aigw setup --from team.toml --dry-run
  aigw setup --from team.toml --provider dmxapi --token-stdin

Options
      --account string          Account ID; guided setup uses the first Route ID when omitted
      --anthropic-url string    Anthropic base URL
      --chat-url string         OpenAI Chat Completions base URL
      --dry-run                 Show what setup would change without reading a Token or writing anything
      --for string              Client for the first route: claude, claude-desktop, codex, or hermes
      --from string             Apply a team file: its providers, models, families and recommendations
  -h, --help                    help for setup
      --json                    Write the setup result as JSON
      --label string            Provider display name
      --openai-url string       OpenAI Responses base URL
      --protocol string         Endpoint protocol when more than one URL is configured: anthropic, responses, or chat
      --provider stringArray    With --from, a provider whose Token to read, at a prompt or from --token-stdin; repeatable
      --prune                   With --from, remove the local models that no client selects and no recommendation names, and unused families
      --route string            First route ID
      --token-stdin             Read one Token from standard input; with --from, the one --provider's
      --upstream-model string   Exact provider model ID for --for
-- refusal.txt --
AIGW  Action required
────────────────────────────────────────

Problem
  Token validation failed: Claude authentication was rejected (HTTP 401)

Fix
  Pipe a Token that the provider accepts into the same command.
